WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.630
Inherited will...

3
00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.540
the tides of time,
and humanity's dreams...

4
00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:20.370
They cannot be stopped.

5
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.480
As long as people seek freedom,

6
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.110
these things will never cease to be.

7
00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.400
Now tell me...

8
00:01:58.260 --> 00:01:59.860
where Crocodile is!

9
00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:06.270
<b>Rainbase, the City of Dreams</b>

10
00:02:04.250 --> 00:02:08.940
Luffy-san is absolutely right. 
I've made up my mind now.

11
00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.940
Let's head to Crocodile's location!

12
00:02:13.180 --> 00:02:14.200
Yeah!

13
00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.660
That certainly seems to be 
the quickest route.

14
00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:21.620
Meaning no more of this annoying, 
roundabout traveling.

15
00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:25.000
So, where is this damn Crocodile?

16
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.790
Let's see here...

17
00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:29.750
This is Alubarna, the capital city 
where my father rules.

18
00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.260
And the Rebel Army is currently here,
preparing to invade Alubarna.

19
00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.220
So we need to take care of Crocodile
before that can happen.

20
00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:43.640
Crocodile is here. Rainbase.

21
00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.510
Rainbase...

22
00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.610
It's about a day's walk north of here.

23
00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.290
C'mon, 
I told you two to quit moaning!

24
00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.820
You get to ride the camel, 
so you can't complain!

25
00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.750
Yeah! Let us ride, too!

26
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:09.240
You camel-woman!

27
00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:10.750
Nami-mel!

28
00:03:09.980 --> 00:03:10.750
Good one!

29
00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.660
Chopper! You haven't 
collapsed today!

30
00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.130
Yeah. I'm gonna try extra hard.

31
00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:19.220
Vivi. Does Rainbase have water?

32
00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:21.700
Yes, there's no problem there.

33
00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.430
It's a gambling town, 
detached from the Rebellion.

34
00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:26.890
Ooh! Gambling?!

35
00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.860
Hey, now! What're you thinking?!

36
00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:33.320
I guess there are carefree cities 
even here in Arabasta.

37
00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:36.200
Gum-Gum No Way!

38
00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:40.320
No! No! No!

39
00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:41.580
Gimme some!

40
00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.450
Gum-Gum No Way!

41
00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:48.250
C'mon! Just a sip! 
This is why we have it!

42
00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:53.740
That dry old guy spent all night 
digging this water up!

43
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.430
We can't just drink it like 
it's nothing, you dumbhead!

44
00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.220
Wow! There are times you 
can restrain yourself!

45
00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:05.240
Of course I can! How rude!

46
00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:06.680
You're rude!

47
00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:10.450
Can't take another step... W-Water...

48
00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.400
So?! How long until Rainbase?!

49
00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.110
Luffy-san.

50
00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.530
Thanks. I never could have 
made this decision on my own.

51
00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.280
Then gimme food.

52
00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:22.990
Huh?

53
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:27.790
After I kick Crocodile's ass, 
gimme food till I burst!

54
00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.500
Okay! I promise!

55
00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:36.550
<b>Rebel Army Camp in Katorea</b>

56
00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:47.310
<b>Kappa
Nanohana Shoeshine Boy</b>

57
00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.310
Please, Koza! Let me join 
the Rebel Army!

58
00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.680
Not a chance.

59
00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:53.000
Why not?! I have the right 
to join the Rebellion too, don't I?!

60
00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:55.690
I despise the king! 
Let me fight with you!

61
00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.010
Show him, Farafla.

62
00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:05.370
He got this protecting me 
in the middle of a battle.

63
00:05:05.370 --> 00:05:07.750
Wanna see the medical tents 
and graves, too?

64
00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.210
Th-That doesn't scare me!

65
00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.940
Towns dried up, and many people 
died 'cause the king stole the rain!

66
00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.010
And I got lotsa friends 
who got sick from it!

67
00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:21.760
It's all the king's fault!

68
00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:24.110
I wanna fight too!

69
00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.720
I'm not afraid of getting 
hurt or even dying!

70
00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.630
Then leave. Our opinions 
are too different.

71
00:05:29.630 --> 00:05:32.230
We're all afraid, 
and none of us want to fight.

72
00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:34.310
Then why do you fight?!

73
00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:38.800
It's not that we want to. 
We have to.

74
00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.940
This country needs us to.

75
00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.210
Whether you get it or not, 
it's got nothing to do with you.

76
00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:45.310
Leave.

77
00:05:46.280 --> 00:05:50.750
I told you to leave, dammit! 
This is no place for kids!

78
00:05:54.170 --> 00:05:55.250
What's wrong, Koza?

79
00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:59.700
It's not like you to lose your temper at children.

80
00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:03.680
It was like looking 
at my old self. It really got to me.

81
00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:10.180
I haven't changed at all...

82
00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.870
Do we have enough weapons?

83
00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.060
No. It's proving difficult...

84
00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.020
Spread the word to the other towns.

85
00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:20.150
As soon as we're armed and ready,

86
00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.820
we launch an all out 
assault on Alubarna!

87
00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:26.340
<b>Alubarna Palace</b>

88
00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:29.640
Sire! It's only a matter of time until 
the Rebel Army attacks Alubarna!

89
00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.910
We must take action 
before it's too late!

90
00:06:31.910 --> 00:06:34.920
Silence! I told you no!

91
00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:38.750
This is not a children's quarrel! 
Is retaliation what you want?!

92
00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.260
But, Your Majesty, at this rate,
the country will be in mortal danger!

93
00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:44.270
And what of it?

94
00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:46.980
It's been clear since 
the dance powder incident

95
00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:51.140
that someone is trying 
to destroy our country!

96
00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.020
You want to 
destroy our countrymen

97
00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:56.230
without knowing who's 
pulling the strings?

98
00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:59.050
That would be
the destruction of this country.

99
00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:01.820
Listen! A country is its people!

100
00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.990
However, the mastermind has 
not yet revealed who they are.

101
00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:09.480
This shadow will devour our country,
and then it will be too late!

102
00:07:10.860 --> 00:07:13.330
No. Please understand.

103
00:07:13.650 --> 00:07:16.330
The king won't allow us 
to take the offensive.

104
00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:20.540
We can barely even appease 
the soldiers at this point.

105
00:07:20.540 --> 00:07:24.510
If only Igaram-san were here 
at a time like this...

106
00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:28.890
Igaram says he's leaving 
the country for a while?

107
00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:37.600
<b>Lt. Chaka "the Jackal"
(Acting Commander)
Arabasta Royal Guard</b>
<b>Lt. Pell "the Falcon"
Arabasta Royal Guard</b>

108
00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:32.050
As we speak, he and Princess Vivi

109
00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:36.190
are probably still hard at work, 
trying to figure out who's behind this.

110
00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:37.770
I wonder where they are.

111
00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.090
Sir Chaka! Sir Pell!

112
00:07:40.090 --> 00:07:41.230
What is it?!

113
00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:43.280
Karoo has returned!

114
00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.940
He has?!

115
00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.900
Sire! Who is that letter from?!

116
00:07:58.790 --> 00:08:01.790
It's Vivi's handwriting, 
without a doubt...

117
00:08:02.260 --> 00:08:04.510
Sire! Does that mean–

118
00:08:04.510 --> 00:08:06.630
Karoo delivered a letter from Vivi?!

119
00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:15.020
Father. Everything written here 
is true. It is fact.

120
00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:25.770
The person trying to bring suffering 
and ruin to this kingdom

121
00:08:25.770 --> 00:08:28.910
is none other than Crocodile!

122
00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:40.500
Igaram is yet another who has fallen 
at the hands of Crocodile.

123
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:44.890
Crocodile! I stupidly believed 
he worked for the government!

124
00:08:44.890 --> 00:08:48.510
I never would have imagined he was 
trying to usurp the throne!

125
00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:51.000
Igaram-san...

126
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:54.850
He gave his life for Princess Vivi 
and this land...

127
00:08:55.830 --> 00:09:02.400
And now, there are powerful people 
lending me their strength.

128
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:06.470
If I continue with them, we can 
make a difference in this kingdom.

129
00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:11.610
The light of hope is here! 
Arabasta will be saved!

130
00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:14.400
Please have faith, Father!

131
00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:15.520
Vivi.

132
00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:26.710
It says you fought valiantly, 
too, Karoo. You've done well.

133
00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:29.850
You were injured? Let me see.

134
00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.620
Anyway, no matter what happens,

135
00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.600
our left arms prove 
we're definitely crewmates!

136
00:09:39.660 --> 00:09:40.600
Chaka.

137
00:09:41.940 --> 00:09:45.560
We know now who our enemy is! 
Prepare the soldiers to march!

138
00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:48.860
Neither Vivi's resolve 
nor Igaram's death will be in vain!

139
00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:50.730
We act immediately!

140
00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:53.070
We're heading to 
Crocodile's home, Rainbase!

141
00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:59.160
Please wait, sire! Rainbase is too far 
away for anything to be "immediate"!

142
00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:02.040
Crocodile presently has 
the support of the populace.

143
00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:06.540
With all due respect, 
even more so than you.

144
00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:09.410
If we attack Rainbase,

145
00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:13.600
the Rebel Army will use 
that as a chance to storm the palace!

146
00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:14.470
If that happens–

147
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:19.890
And so what if the Rebel Army
were to take the palace?!

148
00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.850
I've told you before! 
A country is its people!

149
00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:30.490
Even if the Royal Army falls, 
as long as Crocodile is defeated,

150
00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:33.030
the citizens will rebuild their country!

151
00:10:33.800 --> 00:10:36.990
But, consider if we clash 
with the Rebel Army instead!

152
00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:40.730
Crocodile will assuredly 
have the last laugh!

153
00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.460
Sire...

154
00:10:45.460 --> 00:10:47.210
You're that dedicated to–

155
00:10:47.210 --> 00:10:50.250
Even if by some chance 
the Rebel Army doesn't stop,

156
00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:52.670
we need only take out Crocodile!

157
00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:57.390
We're up against one of 
the Seven Warlords of the Sea.

158
00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.960
Crocodile is not weak willed.

159
00:10:59.960 --> 00:11:04.390
This battle will not be 
without sacrifices before its end.

160
00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:08.360
Chaka! I'm holding a war meeting! 
Assemble the officers!

161
00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.600
Pell! Go on ahead and 
conduct reconnaissance!

162
00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.230
Yes, sire!

163
00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:16.240
It seems we've been severely 
underestimating His Majesty.

164
00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:18.780
What powerful spirit!

165
00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:20.700
We go to battle tomorrow morning!

166
00:11:21.290 --> 00:11:22.370
Yes, sire!

167
00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:25.710
Deploy all soldiers to Rainbase!

168
00:11:36.930 --> 00:11:38.680
I see it...

169
00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:39.800
Is that it?

170
00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.680
Rainbase?

171
00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:46.440
Oh! Did we make it?!

172
00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:48.900
Crocodile!

173
00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:52.690
Alright! Time to beat up Crocodile!

174
00:11:56.890 --> 00:11:59.570
So this is Rainbase!

175
00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:05.500
By the way, does Baroque Works 
know we're in this country now?

176
00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:06.540
Most likely.

177
00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:12.420
We ran into Mr. 2, so we 
should assume they know we're here.

178
00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:13.940
So what?!

179
00:12:13.940 --> 00:12:15.720
They know what we look like!

180
00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:18.800
We can't do much of anything 
while we're in Rainbase!

181
00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.500
Why not?!

182
00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:23.000
If we get spotted first,

183
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:26.390
Crocodile can use just about 
any method to take us out.

184
00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:29.600
Assassination 
is their area of specialty.

185
00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:33.230
Come out, Crocodile!

186
00:12:33.230 --> 00:12:34.650
Were you even listening?!

187
00:12:34.650 --> 00:12:37.000
In any case, no matter 
who we run into,

188
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:40.370
I'll protect Nami-san and Vivi-chan !

189
00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:43.160
You two girls can call me "Prince"!

190
00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:44.840
Prince.

191
00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.500
Don't make me kick your ass!

192
00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:48.960
– Prince... Water... 
– Water...

193
00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.910
Shut up, you guys!

194
00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.840
Water! Need water!

195
00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:54.310
Me too!

196
00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:55.960
Water! Water!

197
00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:55.960
Wait! Luffy!

198
00:12:55.960 --> 00:12:58.300
Take money with you!

199
00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:02.970
<b>Rainbase, the City of Dreams</b>

200
00:13:07.960 --> 00:13:09.430
Captain Smoker.

201
00:13:09.430 --> 00:13:13.630
Why do you think the Straw Hats 
will show up here in Rainbase?

202
00:13:13.630 --> 00:13:15.820
Dunno. Call it intuition.

203
00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:17.810
Alright!

204
00:13:17.810 --> 00:13:20.450
We can get water here, Usopp!

205
00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:20.450
Water!

206
00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:23.570
Plus, something stinks 
about this country.

207
00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:26.480
I've got a hunch something big 
is lurking in the shadows.

208
00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:28.200
Old lady! Water!

209
00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:32.170
A barrel of water! No, five! 
Five barrels of water!

210
00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:34.490
Do you think there really 
is a connection

211
00:13:34.490 --> 00:13:39.260
between the Baroque Works 
criminal organization and Straw Hat?

212
00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.670
Here!

213
00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:46.100
All I know is that Straw Hat 
is out to get Crocodile,

214
00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:51.690
one of the Seven Warlords.

215
00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:51.690
This water's great, you jerk!

216
00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:54.140
It's great, you bastard!

217
00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:58.170
Let's hurry and take some 
to the others!

218
00:14:15.380 --> 00:14:18.380
I need to take a leak.

219
00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:21.420
Can we really count on them?

220
00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:24.340
They can do little errands 
just fine. Don't worry.

221
00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:29.100
I dunno. I bet they'll come back 
with a buncha trouble again.

222
00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:31.020
I'd do warm-up exercises 
if I were you.

223
00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:32.850
Run!

224
00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:32.850
Yeah!

225
00:14:32.850 --> 00:14:34.000
Got that barrel?!

226
00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:34.000
Yeah!

227
00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.180
Damn it! We're going after 'em, 
Tashigi! Gather the marines!

228
00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:37.820
Yes, sir!

229
00:14:38.450 --> 00:14:40.490
Um, how much do I owe you?

230
00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:44.460
If you know those kids, you better 
pay for the water they took, too!

231
00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:46.620
Y-Yes! I'm sorry for the trouble!

232
00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:49.240
Why is the Navy here?!

233
00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:54.250
How should I know?! Just run!

234
00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:00.010
The Navy's chasing 'em again!

235
00:15:00.010 --> 00:15:01.410
No way!

236
00:15:01.410 --> 00:15:03.720
So why are they running this way?!

237
00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:06.720
Hey! Tony-kun hasn't come back yet!

238
00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:09.140
Don't worry! He'll manage!

239
00:15:09.140 --> 00:15:11.600
Hey, guys! The Navy's here!

240
00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.060
You're the one bringing them here!

241
00:15:14.060 --> 00:15:16.350
Catch 'em for sure this time!

242
00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.860
They're quick to run away, 
I'll give 'em that!

243
00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.360
This isn't a good idea!

244
00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.230
Baroque Works is gonna spot us...

245
00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:28.950
if we run through the city!

246
00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:36.790
I think it's too late for that.

247
00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:39.700
Then it's decided! Let's go!

248
00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:39.700
Huh?!

249
00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:41.500
To where Crocodile is!

250
00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.210
Right, Vivi?!

251
00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:48.600
Yes! Do you see that 
alligator-roofed building up ahead?!

252
00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:51.290
That's Crocodile's casino:

253
00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:53.640
Rain Dinners!

254
00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:57.350
There, huh?! So that's 
where Crocodile is?!

255
00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.400
It'd be best if we split up!

256
00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:01.900
It looks that way!

257
00:16:01.900 --> 00:16:04.110
Alright! See you later!

258
00:16:04.110 --> 00:16:05.530
Yeah!

259
00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:08.360
Let's meet at the gator house!

260
00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:09.470
They split up!

261
00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:10.660
Don't let 'em escape!

262
00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:12.620
Come and get me, Smokey!

263
00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:14.830
You got real guts!

264
00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:17.660
Don't think you can 
keep running forever!

265
00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:19.600
White Vine!

266
00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:27.170
Gum-Gum Balloon!

267
00:16:35.870 --> 00:16:37.350
That was close!

268
00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:41.520
Damn!

269
00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.150
Whoops!

270
00:16:44.220 --> 00:16:46.820
Mr. Bushido! This direction, too!

271
00:16:47.380 --> 00:16:49.940
It's them! No doubt about it!

272
00:16:49.940 --> 00:16:51.300
Kill 'em!

273
00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:53.280
The Baroque Works millions!

274
00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:57.650
A tiger at the front gate 
and a wolf at the back, huh?

275
00:16:57.650 --> 00:16:59.210
Go on without me!

276
00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:00.010
Hurry!

277
00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:01.270
R-Right!

278
00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:06.000
Usopp!

279
00:17:06.000 --> 00:17:07.510
Look after Nami-san !

280
00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:08.800
What?!

281
00:17:08.800 --> 00:17:10.970
I'll hold 'em off!

282
00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:13.660
You can count on me!

283
00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:14.960
Sanji-kun...

284
00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:15.850
We are!

285
00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:20.190
Without that smoke freak around, 
they're nothing to worry about.

286
00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:23.060
My deepest condolences.

287
00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:38.660
I hope Mr. Bushido will be all right!

288
00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:46.630
Is that all you got? 
Try again some other time.

289
00:17:47.710 --> 00:17:51.470
Roronoa Zoro! We meet again!

290
00:17:52.510 --> 00:17:54.970
That voice...

291
00:17:55.450 --> 00:17:58.030
I've been looking 
for you a long time!

292
00:17:58.030 --> 00:18:00.810
Where do you get off
cutting down regular citizens?!

293
00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:03.190
There's more going on here than it seems!

294
00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:07.090
Besides, I have no 
desire to fight you!

295
00:18:07.090 --> 00:18:09.820
We settled our match in Loguetown!

296
00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:11.150
No, we didn't!

297
00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:14.260
I haven't even landed 
a single blow yet!

298
00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:17.160
She looks like her! 
Way too much like her!

299
00:18:17.360 --> 00:18:19.620
And quit it with that face, will ya?!

300
00:18:20.310 --> 00:18:24.300
C-Come again?! You're still 
trying to ridicule me?!

301
00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:26.000
You will pay for this!

302
00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:29.380
Dammit! She's the one person 
I can't deal with!

303
00:18:30.530 --> 00:18:31.800
Wait!

304
00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:38.810
Bastards! Get back here!

305
00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:42.390
No!

306
00:18:44.440 --> 00:18:46.480
It's definitely them!

307
00:18:50.280 --> 00:18:51.960
W-We did it!

308
00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:53.240
Way to go, Usopp!

309
00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:57.050
Look! Up ahead! 
The entrance to Rain Dinners!

310
00:18:57.050 --> 00:18:59.400
It's in the middle of a lake!

311
00:19:00.890 --> 00:19:03.250
Is no one here yet?!

312
00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:05.880
Alright! Let's blast 'em!

313
00:19:05.880 --> 00:19:07.460
Start with those two!

314
00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.960
The enemy?!

315
00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:11.880
Zoro!

316
00:19:11.880 --> 00:19:14.130
Wasn't Vivi with you?!

317
00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.590
Yeah! Is she not here yet?!

318
00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:19.360
She might've gone inside!

319
00:19:19.360 --> 00:19:21.330
Let's hurry, then!

320
00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:23.610
Luffy!

321
00:19:23.610 --> 00:19:24.550
Get back here!

322
00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:25.560
Smoke-Smoke's there!

323
00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:28.400
Hey! Let's go! Run inside, guys!

324
00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:30.730
We're going in?

325
00:19:33.460 --> 00:19:35.400
He's in there,

326
00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.360
isn't he?!

327
00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:41.740
Oh? Vivi and the pirates 
are here in town?

328
00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:45.330
Yes. We just received word 
from the millions.

329
00:19:55.430 --> 00:19:58.430
Go welcome the foolish rats.

330
00:19:58.430 --> 00:20:00.010
Yes, sir.

331
00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:07.600
Listen, Crocodile! 
I'm gonna kick your ass!

332
00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.290
I'm coming for you!
